{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1176012-spellcasting-in-the-supernal","id":1176012,"title":"Spellcasting in the Supernal","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-14T11:47:19-08:00","id":1176012,"title":"Spellcasting in the Supernal","content":"An archmage enters his Cintamani. Normally this is used for Imperium rites, but let's say he wants to cast a spell (Imperial or regular). Imperial Mysteries doesn't seem to touch on the idea of casting spells while in the Supernal Realms, but wouldn't it still be possible? My current thought is to treat the Cintamani as a +1 Environment Yantra that also gives rote quality on the spellcasting roll. However, the mage must also roll a rote dice pool based on their Gnosis-derived Paradox. Every success on that roll causes 1 point of Aponoia.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T23:31:36-08:00","id":1176199,"title":"","content":"On what target would you cast within the supernal? I personally think Imperium rites are basically spellcasting within the supernal or the closest thing to it. Spellcasting draws supernal symbolism into the fallen world.... in the supernal its allready there you can just change it around directly, which for all intends and purposes is an Imperium Rite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T00:50:55-08:00","id":1176207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1176012-spellcasting-in-the-supernal?p=1176199#post1176199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On what target would you cast within the supernal? I personally think Imperium rites are basically spellcasting within the supernal or the closest thing to it. Spellcasting draws supernal symbolism into the fallen world.... in the supernal its allready there you can just change it around directly, which for all intends and purposes is an Imperium Rite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Supernal natives, other archmages or ascended in the Supernal, sympathetic casting out of the Supernal (which is probably a Wisdom violation and definitely a Pax violation due to the Abyss possibly entering the Supernal). In some ways, casting spells in the Supernal would be similar to symbolically manipulating the Astral. Except way more powerful. Which at that point might as well just be Imperium.<br /> <br /> It is probably better to only allow Imperium in the Cintamani. But it would be nice if it had at least one mechanical use besides that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T09:47:32-08:00","id":1176305,"title":"","content":"Well the only thing I can see is sympathetically casting out of the Cintamani into any part of the fallen world, everything else should imo be an imperium rite. In the case of casting a mundane spell into the fallen from the supernal I'd give out a +5 bonus to the roll from being in the freaking supernal that does not count as a yantra and roll one die to check for aponoia (perhaps increasing to two dice like paradox if done more than once per scene). Oh and yeah the spell should get warped by alot of paradox dice which you probably cannot (or at least should not) contain....<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T12:19:16-08:00","id":1176344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1176012-spellcasting-in-the-supernal?p=1176305#post1176305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the only thing I can see is sympathetically casting out of the Cintamani into any part of the fallen world, everything else should imo be an imperium rite. In the case of casting a mundane spell into the fallen from the supernal I'd give out a +5 bonus to the roll from being in the freaking supernal that does not count as a yantra and roll one die to check for aponoia (perhaps increasing to two dice like paradox if done more than once per scene). Oh and yeah the spell should get warped by alot of paradox dice which you probably cannot (or at least should not) contain....<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I took your idea and tweaked it a bit. I added the possibility of casting spells directly within the Cintamani as long as the subject is something whose origins lie in the Fallen World, which will usually mean either yourself or another archmage. I also kept the rote quality on the spellcasting roll. I modeled the Tilt after the Shattered Time tilt from Dark Eras - Sundered World. Here are the proposed rules:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> An archmage can also use the Cintamani to cast spells of the Common or Imperial Practices on any subject within the Cintamani whose origins lie in the Fallen World (such as another archmage). Alternatively, they can sympathetically cast to anywhere in the Fallen World viia the Sympathetic Range Attainment. Using the Cintamani this way is empowering, but highly dangerous: casting spells in the Cintamani applies the Supernal Spellcasting Tilt. The Cintamani can also be used as a +1 Environment Yantra for any spells that relate to the symbols it was formed from (in addition to the effects of the Tilt).<br /> <br /> The Cintamani cannot be used to cast spells on subjects outside of it in the Supernal, Supernal symbols, realms, natives, or Ascended mages. To affect the universe in this way requires the use of Imperium.<br /> <br /> <b>Supernal Spellcasting (Tilt):</b> When casting a spell of the Common or Imperial Practices in a Cintamani, the archmaster gains a +5 bonus to the spellcasting roll, and the roll gains the rote quality. However, the archmaster might generate both Aponoia and Paradox. For Aponoia, the archmaster rolls 1 die, plus 1 more die for each spell previously cast in the Scene. Each success on this roll generates 1 point of Aponoia. If the spell crosses the Abyss, it has a base Paradox pool as appropriate for the mage\u2019s Gnosis. If the spell risks Paradox in any way, the Paradox roll has the rote quality. More dangerously, the archmage cannot spend Mana to reduce the Paradox dice pool. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","user":"projectmoon","date":". 01-15-2018, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T12:50:39-08:00","id":1176356,"title":"","content":"Looks good, though I would probably give the Paradox roll rote quality by default. You are sending a spell from the supernal to the fallen world, which requires it to outright cross the abyss..... then again one could argue such is allways the case, so perhaps no additional paradox penalties are necessary. Really the possiblity for Aponoia seems to be the preeminent danger in doing this no matter how you look at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T13:03:28-08:00","id":1176362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1176012-spellcasting-in-the-supernal?p=1176356#post1176356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looks good, though I would probably give the Paradox roll rote quality by default. You are sending a spell from the supernal to the fallen world, which requires it to outright cross the abyss..... then again one could argue such is allways the case, so perhaps no additional paradox penalties are necessary. Really the possiblity for Aponoia seems to be the preeminent danger in doing this no matter how you look at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Paradox roll, if it occurs, has rote quality. With these rules, it's possible to cast spells on targets in the Cintamani, which means they're not across the Abyss. Magic originates in the Supernal, so unless you Reach too much or cast sympathetically across the Abyss into the Fallen, you wouldn't cause a Paradox in my view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","user":"projectmoon","date":". 01-15-2018, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T00:08:37-08:00","id":1176474,"title":"","content":"Here's another thing I was thinking about. Verges, Demenses, and Emanations do not have Paradox risk unless you cast out of them into a realm that does have Paradox risk. Does it not make sense that casting within the Cintamani would also not have Paradox risk? Only casting across the Abyss would cause Paradox. I think the sacrificing of a Willpower dot (i.e. spending 1 XP) and the risk of aponoia may be enough to argue that a Paradox roll is not necessary unless casting across the Abyss. I would perhaps increase the aponoia risk in this case.<br /> <br /> Here is a reworked version of the Tilt that takes this into account:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Supernal Spellcasting (Tilt):</b> When casting a spell of the Common or Imperial Practices in their Cintamani, the archmaster gains a +5 bonus to the spellcasting roll, and the roll gains the rote quality. However, the archmaster might create Aponoia. The archmaster rolls his Gnosis-derived Paradox as a dice pool, plus 1 more die for each spell previously cast in the Scene. Each success on this roll generates 1 point of Aponoia. Casting in the Supernal normally does not risk Paradox, but if the spell crosses the Abyss, it has a base Paradox pool as appropriate for the mage\u2019s Gnosis, in addition to any other Paradox. The Paradox dice pool has the rote quality. More dangerously, the archmage cannot spend Mana to reduce the Paradox dice pool. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}